s a theatre production.</rdfs:comment>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#countryHasCity">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>    <rdfs:label>country has city</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>Inverse: links a country to the cities it contains.</rdfs:comment>    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Country"/>    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#City"/>    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#locatedInCountry"/>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#EnsembleMembership">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>    <rdfs:label>Ensemble Membership</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>A reified relation linking a person to an ensemble with a time period.</rdfs:comment>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#productionRoleTime">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>    <rdfs:label>production role time</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>The time period for which a production role assignment is valid.</rdfs:comment>    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#ProductionRoleAssignment"/>    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#productionRoleActor">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>    <rdfs:label>production role actor</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>Links a production role assignment to the actor.</rdfs:comment>    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#ProductionRoleAssignment"/>    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Actor"/>    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#actorHasProductionRoleAssignment"/>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#hasReview">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>    <rdfs:label>has review</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>Links a production to a review.</rdfs:comment>    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Production"/>    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Review"/>    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#isReviewOf"/>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nfc665b9f66ce49659b1a74ce7c08ba36b1">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#hasPremier"/>    <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</owl:cardinality>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#isEnsembleOf">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>    <rdfs:label>is ensemble of</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>Inverse: links an ensemble to the production it belongs to.</rdfs:comment>    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Ensemble"/>    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Production"/>    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#hasEnsemble"/>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#takesPlaceIn">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>    <rdfs:label>takes place in</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>Alternative property linking a theatre festival to its city.</rdfs:comment>    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#TheatreFestival"/>    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#City"/>    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#isPlaceOf"/>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology/theatre-productions">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"/>    <rdfs:label>Theatre Productions Ontology</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>Ontology for representing theatre festivals, productions, plays, people, and reviews in Italy as described in the theatre productions story.</rdfs:comment>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#Role">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>    <rdfs:label>Role</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>A character or function performed by an actor in a production.</rdfs:comment>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#givenBy">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>    <rdfs:label>given by</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>Links a review to the newspaper that published it.</rdfs:comment>    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Review"/>    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Newspaper"/>    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#publishesReview"/>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#Act">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>    <rdfs:label>Act</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>A major division within a play.</rdfs:comment>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#cityHasTheatre">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>    <rdfs:label>city has theatre</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>Inverse: links a city to the theatres it contains.</rdfs:comment>    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#City"/>    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Theatre"/>    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#locatedInCity"/>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#Theatre">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>    <rdfs:label>Theatre</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>A physical location where theatre productions are held.</rdfs:comment>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#Newspaper">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>    <rdfs:label>Newspaper</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>A periodical publication that may publish reviews.</rdfs:comment>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#roleHasProductionRoleAssignment">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>    <rdfs:label>role has production role assignment</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>Inverse: links a role to production role assignments.</rdfs:comment>    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Role"/>    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#ProductionRoleAssignment"/>    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#productionRoleRole"/>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#isActOf">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>    <rdfs:label>is act of</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>Inverse: links an act to the play it belongs to.</rdfs:comment>    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Act"/>    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Play"/>    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#hasAct"/>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#employedSince">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>    <rdfs:label>employed since</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>The date and time when an actor started working at a theatre.</rdfs:comment>    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Actor"/>    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime"/>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#isAuthorOf">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>    <rdfs:label>is author of</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>Inverse: links an author to the plays they wrote.</rdfs:comment>    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Author"/>    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#Play"/>    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://www.example.org/ontology#hasAuthor"/>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#Country">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>    <rdfs:label>Country</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>A country containing cities.</rdfs:comment>  </rdf:Description>  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.example.org/ontology#TheatreFestival">    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>    <rdfs:label>Theatre Festival</rdfs:label>    <rdfs:comment>A festival event where multiple theatre productions are performed.</rdfs:comment>  </rdf:Description></rdf:RDF>